course: dictionary
lesson: 13542
title: Impracticability: when a plan just won't work
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Impracticability is a long, formal word, but you can break it into parts. Im- means not, practic- is linked to practical (able to be done), and -ability means the quality of. So impracticability is the quality of not being able to be done in real life. «The impracticability of the plan meant it had to be dropped.» The plan could not really be carried out.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Owing to its impracticability, the trip to the Moon was cancelled.» Cancelled tells you the trip could not go ahead, so impracticability must mean it could not be done. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The trip was cancelled because it just would not work.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Formal writers use this word where everyday speech says «it just won't work». Think of the -ability ending: it names a quality, a thing you can point to, so it often follows the, as in the impracticability of.
fact: Impracticability is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say the impracticability, not an impracticability.
fact: Im- means not, practic- links to practical, and -ability means the quality of.
fact: «Impracticability» means the quality of being impossible, or almost impossible, to do in practice.
fact: In formal writing it can mean something that cannot be done because of real limits such as cost, time or difficulty.
fact: Useful phrases: the impracticability of, owing to its impracticability.
exercise: «The impracticability of the plan meant it was dropped.» What does impracticability mean here? | *The plan could not really be carried out | The plan was written in a hurry | Its quality of being a great success | The plan was too colourful to see
exercise: «Owing to its impracticability, the trip to the Moon was cancelled.» Which is the best meaning in this sentence? | *Something that cannot be done because of real limits like cost or time | A sudden loud noise | A very tasty dessert | A shiny new bicycle
exercise: Which plain phrase means the same as «the impracticability of the plan»? | *The plan just won't work | The plan is too pretty | The plan is a secret | The plan is finished early
test: Which part of impracticability means «not»? | practic- | -ability | *im- | -ing
test: In «the impracticability of the plan», what kind of word is impracticability? | a verb | an adverb | *a noun | an adjective
exam: Which sentence uses impracticability correctly? | Yesterday impracticability was sweet and purple | The impracticability ran happily across the field | *The impracticability of the plan meant it had to be dropped | We ate an impracticability for lunch
